WEBVTT

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.910
Welcome.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:15.750
You'd like to sell this back?

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.620
One moment, please.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:23.080
Let's see,
you brought a game console, a VR set,

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.870
and this...

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:29.870
Uh, the game...
<i>Heartthrob! Virtual Boyfriend</i>.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.040
Is that everything?

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:34.290
Yes...

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:37.200
Huh? What?

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.790
Please wait one moment.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.700
Hey, the system won't register
<i>Heartthrob! Virtual Boyfriend</i>.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.500
What was the title again?

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.410
<i>Heartthrob! Virtual Boyfriend</i>.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:51.830
Ah, we stopped buying that one back.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:52.750
We did?

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:54.500
It was in the daily report.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.950
I'm terribly sorry, Miss.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.790
It seems that
<i>Heartthrob! Virtual Boyfriend...</i>

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:05.000
<i>I get it already!</i>

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.250
RAGE

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.330
This is for you.

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:49.790
Yeah?

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:55.290
32,000 yen? You've been working hard.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:02:00.540
I sold off the black box that I was forced
to give my money to, at a secondhand shop.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:01.450
A what?

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:05.040
In any case,
I want to do everything I can!

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:09.250
Hello to all the hard working
women out there.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:12.540
Do you have days
when you want to badmouth your superiors?

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.250
I know I do!

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:18.700
You know what's perfect for those days?
Death Voice!

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:27.080
What do you think?
You can't understand a word, right?

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:30.160
In other words, there's no evidence
of your badmouthing ways!

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:33.250
Death Voice guarantees your security!

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:38.700
<i>My channel gives easy instructions</i>
<i>on how to use your death voice.</i>

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.200
Hmm... Only 24 viewers?

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:44.620
It's so hard to get advertising revenue.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.660
Slow but steady wins the race, Retsuko.

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:48.040
I'll do my best!

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:54.450
If we insert a design printout here...

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.330
Voilà. It comes out like this...

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:02.040
We can sell this for 400 yen!

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:04.750
Wow, that's great.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:06.160
What's the cost of production?

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:07.250
40 yen each!

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:08.410
Sweet!

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.660
We can also put
our pictures with fans here...

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:15.080
to make special order pins!

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.500
How much will that one cost?

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:19.120
We should mark it up, so...

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:20.790
1,500 yen!

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:22.950
-What? Wait a sec!
-And the cost of production is?

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:23.870
40 yen each!

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:24.950
-Sweet!
-Sweet!

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:26.330
She's a pro!

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:27.870
So greedy!

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:32.950
Fans are always looking for a chance
to waste their money, you know?

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.660
Picking up small change like that
makes us look cheap. I'm not doing it.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.330
I'm doing this
so OTM Girls can turn a profit.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.250
Stop acting like this is below you.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:46.080
I want to try selling our T-shirts, too.
Any good ideas?

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.830
Wear one for a while, and then sell it.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:48.830
Bait for groupies!

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:51.330
We could even put it up for auction.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:52.660
-Sweet!
-Sweet!

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.040
OUTSKIRTS

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.500
A social media account?

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:58.910
Yes, we can use it
to promote our merchandise.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.830
I also think we should update it
as often as possible.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.120
Do you have an official account?

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:09.120
Why, of course.
Just try looking up "OTM Girls" on Gugu.

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:11.250
See?

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:14.790
MANAKA, MIGI AND HIDARIN.
A TRIO BASED IN TOKYO!

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:19.660
Who manages this account?

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:24.290
It's not me. Who manages it? You, Manaka?

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.870
It's not me. Don't you do it, Hidarin?

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:28.620
No. I thought Migi did.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.330
I thought it was you, Mr. Hyodo.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.540
Um... Er...

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.500
I didn't believe it at first,

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:38.910
but I think this account...

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:41.580
is a case of identity fraud.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.330
Identity fraud?

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:44.450
What do you mean?

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:47.000
A stranger puts up
an official-looking account

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:50.370
when, really, an official account
never existed in the first place.

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:51.950
-What?
-Creepy!

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:53.660
Who's writing this?

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:55.750
They're casually taking sneaky shots!

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.200
I thought you were managing that account!

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:01.040
I thought you girls
just went ahead and made--

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.620
Stop!

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.120
We need to handle this properly!

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:08.160
I'll create an official account
for the OTM Girls right now.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:12.370
We'll send out new information
to our fans every day.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.910
I intend to manage it myself.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.290
Is that okay with all of you?

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:19.700
-Please do.
-Yeah...

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:26.000
What? How irresponsible.

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:28.790
Who is this Hyodo guy, anyway?

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:33.120
Well, I don't think this is his main job.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.660
The members
don't know what he does either.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:39.870
You seem to be attached to this side job.

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:42.410
It looks like you're actually enjoying it.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:45.080
I'm doing it for free, though.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:48.910
It's like we're starting from scratch.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.370
Honestly, it's pretty fun...

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:54.790
even though some might think
that we're playing make-believe.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.870
Grown-up jobs are like child's play,
but on a larger scale.

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:00.410
It's just like playing house
or having a secret base.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.200
You might be right.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.750
-Ah, excuse me.
-I'm sorry.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:23.370
-Huh?
-Hmm? Wait...

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:25.000
Haida?

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:29.120
Ah, you're from General Affairs...

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:32.870
Uh...

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.580
Ah, wait! It'll come to me!

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.370
Inui.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:47.200
I didn't expect you
to remember my name, Haida.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.950
And I didn't expect to find you
in a vinyl record shop.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:54.620
I know.
It doesn't suit my appearance, does it?

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:58.040
I also listen to new wave music,
not just punk.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:00.660
I guess we were both born
in the wrong era.

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:02.790
Yeah, I've often thought the same thing!

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:07.580
The music from that generation
is edgier than the music nowadays.

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:11.370
Well, you're right,
but the way you said it was a bit...

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:15.370
Huh? Did I sound too harsh?
How should I describe it?

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.700
-It feels more live?
-It has an analog vibe?

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:20.330
Like an eloquent voice between the notes!

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.950
That doesn't sound right.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.160
I guess edgy is the best way
to describe it, after all.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:30.120
Edgy sounds cool, too, doesn't it?

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.750
<i>O! T! M!</i>

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:45.000
<i>O! T! M!</i>

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:47.540
EVENT INFORMATION: SATURDAY, 19:15
PRE-ORDER TICKET: 2,500 YEN

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:50.080
There! I've finished the announcement!

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:57.750
<i>Ready, set, go!</i>

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:00.290
<i>I want to be a viral star</i>

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.290
<i>On a shiny stage...</i>

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:03.950
<i>We're performing live now!</i>

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:06.370
<i>It may be sad but I still dream</i>

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:08.080
Welcome!

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:09.620
<i>In the darkness of my mind</i>

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:14.540
<i>We don’t need a special future</i>
<i>I don’t care if it’s just fake</i>

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:16.250
That comes to a total of 1,500 yen!

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:18.290
It only cost us 40 yen, though!

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:19.750
Thank you very much!

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:20.660
SOLD OUT

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.200
<i>We're sold out!</i>

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:23.660
SOLD OUT! THANK YOU!

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:31.450
Manaka.

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:35.290
Migi. Hidarin.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:41.700
So, we can earn money
with this job, after all!

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:43.040
It's like a dream.

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:46.410
Accounting manager, here's yours.

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:49.080
I'd hardly call it pocket money, though.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:51.830
Thank you.

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:57.580
I've never received
anything like this before.

00:08:57.830 --> 00:09:01.790
What are you talking about?
You have a monthly salary, don't you?

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:06.410
This is the first time I've felt like
I actually earned the money myself.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:09.660
I can't believe I'm capable of doing this.

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:14.410
Well... you've earned that money.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:15.870
Thank you!

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:17.330
I'm glad you're working with us!

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.870
Your hard work
is what made this possible!

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.660
Huh? Are you forgetting
we're supposed to make money?

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:26.540
It was more unusual that
we didn't in the first place! Moreover--

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:35.290
But, well...
I guess I am grateful for your help.

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:36.910
There we have it!

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:40.500
Well, then, I'll just return this to you.

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:42.910
Please put this
towards the repayment of my debt.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:46.330
Keep it as a memento.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:52.700
From now on, we'll earn more money!

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:54.040
Yeah!

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:56.250
Good!
Now, let's eat some delicious ramen!

00:09:56.330 --> 00:09:57.330
Yay!

00:09:57.410 --> 00:10:01.120
Ramen? That sounds so cheap!

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:19.620
-Really?
-I'm serious!

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:25.750
She just came
to return the record I lent her.

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:28.660
That's it?

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:32.080
We also talked about work problems.

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:35.580
Man, being relied on sure is tiring.

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:38.580
That's it?

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:40.910
What do you want?

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:43.450
You two had good chemistry back there.

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:47.450
Huh? You've got it all wrong, you fool!
It's not like that!

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:57.040
You drink red bean soup now?

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:58.330
No!

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:01.040
That's for you. See you!

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:10.080
So sweet.

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:16.370
Good work, everyone!

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:18.200
Good work.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:31.870
Um, this song... Could it be...

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:35.290
Yeah. It's the demo of our new song.

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:37.750
Really? It sounds nice!

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:39.080
I know, right?

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:42.410
So, Manaka will perform as
the group's center and main singer again?

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.290
Yeah, that's right.

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:47.160
She is great at singing, after all.
I can't wait.

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:56.200
<i>Life is so confusing</i>

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:58.660
<i>My heart is in turmoil</i>

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:09.500
If you want me to sing properly,
then please rent a real studio!

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:12.790
Don't ask for luxuries.
A karaoke room is enough.

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:15.450
It should be around here.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:18.700
We're going all the way to Ōtemachi
just for a karaoke room?

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:20.830
But there are only office buildings here!

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:22.620
I got a free coupon.

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:24.580
From who?

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:32.040
OTM is short for "Ōtemachi," right?

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:37.080
You know, sometimes we make jokes...

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:40.790
"Wouldn't it be funny if Mr. Hyodo
turned out to be an office worker?"

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:45.330
What's your day job, anyway?

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:46.580
Ouch!

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:48.540
It's here.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:51.580
KARAOKE

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:54.790
It smells like cigarettes!

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:56.120
Quit complaining.

00:12:56.370 --> 00:12:57.870
Did you write down the lyrics?

00:12:57.950 --> 00:13:01.750
I did, but how do you
get the music to play here?

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:04.620
It would seem that
you can hook up your smartphone.

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:06.450
Go ahead and set it up.

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:09.370
What? Hey, where are you going?

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:10.750
To the restroom.

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:12.410
Subtitle translation by: Rachael Momber
